                        "sense_id": "d3c4a21f-741b-3f3a-82f1-6ce4095e6df1",
                        "entry_id": "64e4d490-d23c-3075-9879-e8365c78423b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A fan or flabellum."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "63a0db46-a3a4-4e25-b1ef-dde9bc051a7e",
                                "sense_id": "d3c4a21f-741b-3f3a-82f1-6ce4095e6df1",
                                "text": "Moreouer, the lungs which are the flabell of the heart […] are by the immoderate heate and sircitie [fiercity?] of this fume, quickely dried and coarctated, and consequently become vnapt for motion, to the great offence of the heart, and ruine at length of the whole body."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c783ed06-676a-478e-bc7f-b0236f4d1ecd",
                                "sense_id": "d3c4a21f-741b-3f3a-82f1-6ce4095e6df1",
                                "text": "And so this flabel of Schism in the Church, shall also be the bellows of Sedition in the Common-wealth."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6ca4c448-55b3-4b12-9322-374da49371bb",
                                "sense_id": "d3c4a21f-741b-3f3a-82f1-6ce4095e6df1",
                                "text": "The Bramins also distribute Flabels to the most considerable of the Company, the handles whereof being eight foot long, are plated with Gold and Silver. […] There are six of these Flabels usually employ’d to keep off the Flies from their God; the better sort taking it by turns, that the honour of waiting upon their God may be more equally shar’d."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
